WEBVTT

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:08.470
It's in conformance
with the data from LIGO.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:11.020
The reading on the interferometer
is climbing, too.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:11.930
What's the origin?

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:13.770
Report from the Maritime Force.

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:17.310
125 miles northeast of Dogo Island
of the Oki Islands,

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.070
the deserted island Sea Dragon Rock
is starting to swell.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:36.040
Then I'll be leaving the rest to you.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.750
-You can count on us!
-Be careful.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:45.840
Key Girl.

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:55.310
Incoming message from the Yokota COC.

00:00:55.390 --> 00:01:00.070
An aircraft off the Noto Peninsula coast
has emerged. It is the large-scale OTF.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:01.780
It's finally time.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:03.360
<i>Ready to go?</i>

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:04.610
Yes, ma'am!

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:11.290
Roger.

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:15.030
I never thought that old ha--

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:18.410
that Ms. Hinomoto would
come back as a Dragon Pilot.

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:24.750
The suit I developed for Kaizaki
that appeals to OTF came in handy.

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:28.880
<i>OTF Flight, vector 310.</i>

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:31.800
<i>Climb angle 20. Contact channel 1.</i>

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:33.180
<i>Take care.</i>

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:35.470
<i>OTF Flight. Roger.</i>

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:36.890
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:39.850
It begins at last.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:47.110
Entering the storm area momentarily.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:48.860
Oh my goodness.

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:52.030
You're kidding, right?

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:59.790
Remain calm. We've flown
this course before.

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:01.750
We will make it.

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:30.780
Visual contact on the target.

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:35.490
It's been a while...

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.380
He's bigger than Futomomo...

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:55.760
<i>Penguin and Sada, please begin</i>
<i>escorting Lord Mitatsu.</i>

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:57.090
<i>Roger.</i>

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:05.730
<i>He'll snap at you coming from the sides.</i>
<i>Ride his slipstream and face him head on!</i>

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:07.350
<i>Y-Yes, ma'am!</i>

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:34.630
The large-scale OTF is rerouting to 1-5-0.

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:36.010
The escort succeeded.

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:40.800
In that case, shall we go
verify the target?

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:42.890
Maezawa, Kogure,

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:45.520
please contact us if anything happens.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:46.520
Roger!

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:50.440
Please take me with you!

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:55.070
-Airman 3rd Class Kaizaki?
-I want to see their work up close.

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:57.860
I can assist with maintenance
if something happens!

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:00.950
And even if I can't fly,

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:03.040
I am still a Dragon Pilot!

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:04.620
Kaizaki...

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:08.080
Understood. You are permitted
to come along.

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:10.380
Thank you very much!

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:20.550
<i>What are you doing?</i>

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:29.650
<i>I wonder... what she is doing now.</i>

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:36.530
WHAT IS HISONE AMAKASU DOING?

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:39.660
Goro. Purr, purr, purr.

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:42.700
Goro! Purr, purr, purr.

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:46.750
Oh, Goro, why won't you purr for me?

00:06:47.290 --> 00:06:48.750
Goro.

00:06:51.630 --> 00:06:53.840
Hisone gonna be all right?

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:56.590
She came this far, ya know.
She did good.

00:06:56.670 --> 00:06:58.470
She's gotta be hungry, ya?

00:06:58.550 --> 00:07:00.800
Make her some inari sushi.

00:07:01.010 --> 00:07:02.720
<i>I'm making them worry.</i>

00:07:04.010 --> 00:07:05.760
<i>I suddenly quit my job,</i>

00:07:05.890 --> 00:07:08.020
<i>didn't give so much as a reason why,</i>

00:07:08.270 --> 00:07:13.610
<i>and now they're gonna stuff me</i>
<i>some sweet inari sushi.</i>

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:19.030
<i>How did scum like me</i>
<i>come from such a kind couple?</i>

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:22.910
Scum... like me.

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:27.080
You're quitting...
the Air Self-Defense Force?

00:07:27.370 --> 00:07:28.580
Yes. I'm quitting.

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:30.790
H-Hang on a second.

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:33.670
Right now, before the Ritual,
is a critical moment...

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:35.040
Technical Sergeant Amakasu,

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:37.500
How did you arrive to that conclusion?

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:41.180
I like Okonogi!

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:44.180
Y-You don't... mince words.

00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:47.640
Yes. But... I also love Masotan!

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:51.520
There was nothing
that was precious to me before.

00:07:51.940 --> 00:07:53.560
Just my parents, and Goro,

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:57.860
the DeAgostini weekly "Global Western
House" series I'm in the middle of,

00:07:58.030 --> 00:08:00.240
oh, and an autograph
from the athlete Shinjo.

00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:02.400
You have quite a list...

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:04.990
But it's not just Okonogi.

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:06.660
Nao, El,

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:08.200
Hitomi, Lilikos,

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:11.330
Commander Sosoda
and Flight Leader Kakiyasu, too.

00:08:11.410 --> 00:08:13.960
My point is that I've come
to cherish many people now!

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:19.960
If my uncertainty about Okonogi is causing
problems for other people I care about,

00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:21.300
then I can't stand it.

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:22.720
No, no, no,

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:26.090
it's an even bigger problem for us
if you resign now--

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:27.260
However!

00:08:27.470 --> 00:08:30.430
I also cannot stop
my feelings for Okonogi.

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:35.310
And most importantly,
I can't put Masotan in such a tough place.

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:39.400
I want to continue saying that the things
that I cherish are important.

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:42.990
That is why I will quit my position
in the Air Self-Defense Force.

00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:46.820
Don't rush into your decision.

00:08:47.030 --> 00:08:48.950
We can find a way around the anastomo--

00:08:49.030 --> 00:08:50.740
-Understood!
-Huh?

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:53.250
Flight Leader Kakiyasu!

00:08:55.170 --> 00:08:56.710
Pack your bags!

00:08:57.920 --> 00:08:59.710
Flight Leader Kakiyasu--

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:01.800
Did you feel nothing?!

00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:05.380
Towards your training here
or life with your comrades?!

00:09:05.510 --> 00:09:07.090
T-That's what I meant by importa--

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:08.890
Shut up, you scum!

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:13.140
If that's your excuse for quitting
the Air Self-Defense Force,

00:09:13.390 --> 00:09:15.730
then we don't need scum like you here!

00:09:15.810 --> 00:09:16.650
Quit?

00:09:17.810 --> 00:09:18.690
Get the hell out.

00:09:19.150 --> 00:09:20.070
Right now.

00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:24.030
I don't want to see your face!

00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:29.990
Does that mean I'm a bad person?

00:09:30.950 --> 00:09:35.960
No matter how you look at it,
I really am no good.

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:39.420
Ah, Goro!

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:40.920
Goro.

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:45.420
If you go wandering off, you never know
what's out there to get you.

00:09:49.550 --> 00:09:51.050
You're going to get all dusty.

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:57.390
AOKI HIGH SCHOOL TOYAMA, PREFECTURE

00:10:02.730 --> 00:10:05.150
<i>I was out of the loop,</i>
<i>if I say so myself.</i>

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:08.360
<i>I just forced myself in with my peers.</i>

00:10:09.410 --> 00:10:10.570
<i>As far as friends go,</i>

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:13.080
<i>I didn't have a single one.</i>

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:16.540
<i>Going out for drinks,</i>

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:19.290
<i>trading side dishes we didn't like,</i>

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:21.540
<i>stargazing...</i>

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:25.420
<i>going to the movies...</i>

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:28.220
<i>All of it</i>

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:30.010
<i>was a first experience.</i>

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:32.470
JOIN THE SELF-DEFENSE FORCE
TO PROTECT WHAT I CHERISH

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:38.390
<i>Protect what I...</i>

00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:39.900
<i>cherish.</i>

00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:45.730
<i>Hiso Maso!</i>

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:53.450
The large-scale OTF is entering
a stable trajectory.

00:10:53.990 --> 00:10:55.620
Everything is on schedule.

00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:59.870
At this rate, we'll reach
the sleep turnover point smoothly.

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:03.540
This guy is really leisurely.

00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:08.840
Are you thinking about Amakasu?

00:11:10.430 --> 00:11:12.930
I might be dragging it around even now,

00:11:13.510 --> 00:11:17.390
the pain of not being chosen...
to be a Dragon Pilot.

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:21.940
Even your man
was taken by a Dragon Pilot...

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:24.560
Man?

00:11:25.480 --> 00:11:28.740
Regardless, I decided to serve as a member
of the Self-Defense Force

00:11:28.820 --> 00:11:31.700
and support the Dragon Pilots
through training.

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:34.660
That may sound good,

00:11:35.330 --> 00:11:37.790
but my dream remains suspended in limbo,

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:41.370
and I may have affixed it onto
Technical Sergeant Amakasu.

00:11:51.050 --> 00:11:55.760
Technical Sergeant Amakasu's actions are
by no means admirable.

00:11:56.430 --> 00:11:59.930
But for me, it was a blessing.

00:12:02.810 --> 00:12:05.060
Yes. There's a good boy.

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:07.070
Keep moving forward,

00:12:08.190 --> 00:12:10.190
to Yae's side.

00:12:12.070 --> 00:12:13.410
I want you to stop after all.

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:17.450
Even if it's for the country,
the thought of losing you

00:12:17.990 --> 00:12:20.000
is unbearable.

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:22.660
I want to go to Paris.

00:12:23.710 --> 00:12:24.670
Yae...

00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:27.670
All right. Let's go there.

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:29.960
We'll ride the Organic Transformed Fli--

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:31.760
Montparnasse.

00:12:32.340 --> 00:12:34.930
We secretly decided
that's his name, right?

00:12:36.010 --> 00:12:36.850
Yeah.

00:12:37.050 --> 00:12:39.930
Let's ride Montparnasse
and escape to Paris.

00:12:51.650 --> 00:12:52.990
After leaving the village,

00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:55.610
I'm so glad the first friend I made...

00:12:56.410 --> 00:12:57.530
was you.

00:12:58.330 --> 00:12:59.410
Sada, dear.

00:13:09.460 --> 00:13:11.800
We're receiving an emergency signal
from Serpent!

00:13:12.260 --> 00:13:14.260
W-What is going on?!

00:13:14.630 --> 00:13:16.800
It seems that anastomosis has begun.

00:13:16.890 --> 00:13:18.350
Can you hear me, Sada?

00:13:18.550 --> 00:13:20.180
-What's your status--
-<i>Montparnasse.</i>

00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:24.770
Montparnasse, we threw away everything.

00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:29.060
To support you, to fly with you!

00:13:29.560 --> 00:13:30.400
And yet,

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:33.740
why won't you choose me?!

00:13:34.070 --> 00:13:36.990
Are my sins too deep?!

00:13:37.320 --> 00:13:38.740
Montparnasse!

00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:49.000
-Masotan!
-<i>Keep calm!</i>

00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:51.550
<i>Our job is to escort Lord Mitatsu!</i>

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:54.920
Serpent's deviating
from the dragon's route!

00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:56.760
Where is she flying?!

00:13:56.930 --> 00:13:59.800
Forty miles northeast of Komatsu.

00:14:00.140 --> 00:14:03.060
It's closest to...
the Toyama rendezvous point!

00:14:04.930 --> 00:14:08.690
Sada, try to lure the OTF
in that direction.

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:11.900
That girl is in Toyama, isn't she?

00:14:15.110 --> 00:14:17.740
What's this? The rain started so suddenly.

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:20.240
Hisone, come help.

00:14:35.510 --> 00:14:38.630
Oh no! The towel is flying away!

00:14:38.970 --> 00:14:40.720
-I heard it.
-Huh?

00:14:41.930 --> 00:14:44.310
I heard... Masotan's voice!

00:14:46.390 --> 00:14:47.600
Masotan?

00:14:50.850 --> 00:14:53.980
Promptly reserve the rendezvous point
and get official notice.

00:14:54.070 --> 00:14:55.900
F-Flight Leader Kakiyasu!

00:14:56.610 --> 00:14:58.530
There's... a text.

00:14:58.900 --> 00:14:59.740
A text?

00:14:59.820 --> 00:15:01.070
It's from Amakasu!

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:03.740
-Let me see that!
-Hey!

00:15:04.660 --> 00:15:06.080
I'M SORRY!

00:15:06.490 --> 00:15:07.330
I WILL HURRY!

00:15:07.830 --> 00:15:10.080
Oh, the White Lover is...

00:15:10.210 --> 00:15:12.670
Contact her immediately
to get to the rendezvous--

00:15:12.790 --> 00:15:14.630
She is a private citizen!

00:15:15.130 --> 00:15:16.210
Kakiyasu.

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:19.340
Endangering citizens' lives
is a serious offense!

00:15:21.050 --> 00:15:22.760
She ran away!

00:15:25.930 --> 00:15:26.930
I must go.

00:15:28.180 --> 00:15:30.140
It doesn't matter if it's a misconception.

00:15:30.350 --> 00:15:31.900
I must go.

00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:33.310
Because...

00:15:34.060 --> 00:15:35.820
Masotan is calling for me!

00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:39.110
Huh?

00:15:48.200 --> 00:15:49.290
Are you okay?

00:15:54.420 --> 00:15:56.880
F-Flight Leader Kakiyasu.

00:15:56.960 --> 00:15:58.210
Amakasu?!

00:15:58.380 --> 00:15:59.380
Amakasu.

00:15:59.800 --> 00:16:01.510
Why are you here?

00:16:02.010 --> 00:16:06.850
I am very sorry!

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:12.770
Now you want to apologize?

00:16:12.850 --> 00:16:15.690
I wrote that I want to protect
the people I cherish!

00:16:16.940 --> 00:16:19.320
I really hadn't thought about that.

00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:22.740
Like I said before,
there wasn't much I cared about.

00:16:22.900 --> 00:16:24.950
"But why the Air Self-Defense Force?"

00:16:25.030 --> 00:16:27.490
"Because you couldn't get
into other schools, right?"

00:16:27.580 --> 00:16:29.950
I didn't want the other girls
to whisper about me!

00:16:30.040 --> 00:16:33.290
But I was told to write
something I put thought into!

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:36.250
I don't have time for your sob story--

00:16:36.330 --> 00:16:38.000
I didn't understand

00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:40.710
what it was that I cherished

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:42.380
and what to do about it!

00:16:42.470 --> 00:16:46.140
I said I wanted to continue
saying what I cherished,

00:16:46.550 --> 00:16:50.220
But that was not good enough!

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:52.390
You must protect

00:16:52.890 --> 00:16:55.150
the things you cherish!

00:16:56.190 --> 00:16:57.020
Amakasu...

00:16:58.360 --> 00:16:59.900
Are you finished talking?

00:17:00.190 --> 00:17:02.780
K-Kakiyasu...

00:17:03.110 --> 00:17:05.410
Why don't you try
thinking about it calmly?

00:17:05.740 --> 00:17:09.370
We don't have time for people
who can't board the OTF.

00:17:09.450 --> 00:17:12.700
You try thinking calmly about it too,
Flight Leader Kakiyasu!

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:13.870
Huh?

00:17:14.290 --> 00:17:16.500
The people who are important to me,

00:17:16.710 --> 00:17:18.710
everyone, including Okonogi,

00:17:19.090 --> 00:17:21.880
are all people I met through Masotan!

00:17:22.420 --> 00:17:27.470
In other words, I cherish Masotan the most
because he brought us together.

00:17:27.970 --> 00:17:30.010
If I can convey that feeling to Masotan,

00:17:30.680 --> 00:17:33.890
I believe I can definitely board him!

00:17:34.890 --> 00:17:35.770
Please,

00:17:36.350 --> 00:17:40.150
let me ride Masotan one more time!

00:17:42.030 --> 00:17:44.860
You're really good at running your mouth.

00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:48.320
You blurt out what you think immediately.

00:17:48.410 --> 00:17:52.330
To get to the top shelf,
you'll step on others with muddy feet.

00:17:52.910 --> 00:17:55.660
T-That's exactly right, but...

00:17:55.750 --> 00:17:58.710
But you aren't a liar.

00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:02.590
Flight Leader Kakiyasu...

00:18:07.550 --> 00:18:08.800
I'll let you do it.

00:18:10.050 --> 00:18:11.390
I'll let you do all of it.

00:18:11.930 --> 00:18:13.640
Hurry up and board,

00:18:13.720 --> 00:18:15.350
Technical Sergeant Amakasu!

00:18:16.560 --> 00:18:17.850
Kakiyasu.

00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:22.730
Yes, ma'am!

00:18:24.230 --> 00:18:26.900
At present, the OTF is
in an uncontrollable state.

00:18:27.360 --> 00:18:28.990
Add in the weather,

00:18:29.110 --> 00:18:31.870
and a transfer in a best condition
is impossible.

00:18:32.330 --> 00:18:36.000
Therefore, we'll have the OTF
fly at a low elevation,

00:18:36.540 --> 00:18:39.120
and swallow the White Lover like that.

00:18:40.040 --> 00:18:43.210
If this doesn't go well, we can only hope
to be fired and nothing more.

00:18:43.960 --> 00:18:45.000
Masotan,

00:18:46.210 --> 00:18:48.840
Flight Leader Kakiyasu acknowledged me.

00:18:49.630 --> 00:18:50.590
Masotan...

00:18:53.970 --> 00:18:55.390
I'm coming for you,

00:18:55.930 --> 00:18:58.230
Masotan!

00:19:02.480 --> 00:19:04.320
I"m feeling a little weak...

00:19:04.400 --> 00:19:05.400
Go!

00:19:06.360 --> 00:19:09.860
I'm at a disadvantage!

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:25.750
She did it!

00:19:27.920 --> 00:19:31.840
I'm sorry, Masotan!
Everything will be fine now.

00:19:32.640 --> 00:19:36.010
Technical Sergeant Amakasu,
hurry and control him...

00:19:46.570 --> 00:19:48.740
Oh, Masotan!

00:19:48.820 --> 00:19:51.110
You're such a good boy!

00:19:51.200 --> 00:19:52.490
Thank you!

00:19:54.870 --> 00:19:57.040
I can't hold it anymore.
I'm gonna barf.

00:19:57.160 --> 00:20:01.710
Everyone, Technical Sergeant Amakasu
has joined us!

00:20:01.790 --> 00:20:03.670
Please be patient a little longer...

00:20:03.750 --> 00:20:04.830
Amakasu?!

00:20:07.960 --> 00:20:09.960
That girl is dishonest.

00:20:39.240 --> 00:20:41.960
The gravitational vector is fluctuating.

00:20:42.540 --> 00:20:44.620
What exactly is happening?

00:20:53.550 --> 00:20:54.680
It is time.

00:20:55.590 --> 00:20:56.890
The Ritual

00:20:57.180 --> 00:21:02.140
will begin with a song by the miko to put
Lord Mitatsu to sleep.

00:21:02.520 --> 00:21:06.600
Then, by cutting the Shimenawa rope
that ties the two tails,

00:21:06.850 --> 00:21:10.280
the body is rolled over
from top to bottom.

00:21:11.650 --> 00:21:13.650
Be calm, be still,

00:21:13.780 --> 00:21:15.450
behave, be composed.

00:21:16.030 --> 00:21:18.450
-On this night...
-After the rolling,

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:22.080
for a second time,
the miko will ring their bells

00:21:22.160 --> 00:21:25.500
and send Lord Mitatsu
into Fushido, his bedchamber.

00:21:25.870 --> 00:21:29.090
...the Key Girl will serve you,
summon the miko.

00:21:29.750 --> 00:21:34.380
Watch for a thousand years
from the heavens...

00:21:37.470 --> 00:21:39.850
Oh, I can hear them!

00:21:40.350 --> 00:21:41.930
It has begun.

00:21:42.060 --> 00:21:45.180
If all goes well,
it's our turn to do the rolling.

00:21:45.270 --> 00:21:46.350
Yae...

00:21:47.480 --> 00:21:48.690
Ms. Sada?

00:21:48.770 --> 00:21:50.360
P-Please wait!

00:21:50.820 --> 00:21:53.990
<i>Ms. Sada is being a wandering old person!</i>

00:21:55.110 --> 00:21:58.200
Confronting destiny...

00:21:58.740 --> 00:22:00.450
Ms. Sada!

00:22:05.120 --> 00:22:06.290
Yae...

00:22:08.670 --> 00:22:12.130
You're not alone anymore, Yae.

00:22:12.210 --> 00:22:13.630
Ms. Sada?

00:22:13.960 --> 00:22:16.510
I was like you.

00:22:16.920 --> 00:22:20.800
I turned my back on the mission

00:22:21.970 --> 00:22:25.180
because I learned of the truth.

00:22:25.390 --> 00:22:26.890
Truth?

00:22:29.350 --> 00:22:30.810
For the Ritual,

00:22:32.820 --> 00:22:35.030
a sacrifice is required.

00:22:36.280 --> 00:22:38.990
TO BE CONTINUED

00:24:09.660 --> 00:24:13.500
<i>Masotan!</i>

00:24:13.750 --> 00:24:14.670
<i>Masotan.</i>

00:24:18.880 --> 00:24:21.670
<i>I love you!</i>
